IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-elector`

-- Electoral Act 1907 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment, following the Graffiti Vandalism
-- Act encoding's design (D2, D4, D8). Every exported question takes `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"); a
-- question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input, so the site's question
-- form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. Three people the Act puts duties on or gives rights to:
--   - the State elector, or a person who may be entitled to enrol (the baseline's seat): entitlement, enrolment, the
--     duty to vote, the penalty notice (ss 4, 17, 17AA, 18, 31, 31A, 35A, 45, 156), and, as an employee, the right to
--     leave to vote (s 196(1), (2));
--   - the employer of an elector, who must allow leave of absence to vote (s 196);
--   - the candidate, who must lodge a deposit (ss 81, 81A), may withdraw (s 82) and gets the deposit back or loses it
--     (s 84).
-- The Electoral Commissioner, returning officers, the Australian Electoral Officer and the courts are never a seat: what
-- they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking. A registered political party nominates its
-- candidate (s 81A) but is not a seat here; its nomination appears as a fact about the candidate.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8). A question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's fact straight after
-- `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it is FALSE, without reading anything else. The questions of one
-- situation share one input with the same name, type and @desc. There are six, all BOOLEAN:
--   - `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`: the seven elector questions of s 156(6)-(15) (the response
--     date, the modified penalty's cap, the response, the infringement notice, a prosecution after the notice, another
--     elector responding, removal from the register). Each turns on a penalty notice sent under s 156(4);
--   - `I have changed my address within my district`: the two s 45(2) questions, which run from "the change";
--   - `I am on the Commonwealth roll for an address in Western Australia`: the ss 31, 31A, 35A question;
--   - `I am an employee`: the elector's two s 196 questions;
--   - `an employee has asked me for leave to vote`: the employer's three s 196 questions, which turn on the employee's
--     notification (s 196(1));
--   - `the election has been held and the votes counted`: the candidate's s 84 question ("after the election").
-- The other questions arise in every situation of their role and take none.
--
-- The elector's rules are in ea-elector.l4. This module calls them and restates none: for the elector, each answer is
-- the baseline export's own answer, wrapped in this layer's answer types. The employer's and the candidate's rules are
-- not in the baseline; they are written here from the deposited text (ss 81, 81A, 82, 84, 190, 196) as helpers. No
-- exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The layer does no date arithmetic of its own.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Electoral Act 1907 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector`
    `I employ someone who is a State elector`
    `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Hours` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `up to` HAS `hours` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Day answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `by the end of` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no day comes: you are not qualified to be enrolled apart from your age and residence`

DECLARE `Where my Commonwealth enrolment goes` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it reaches the register: your Commonwealth claim is also your State claim, received by the Australian Electoral Officer`
    `it may reach the register: the Electoral Commissioner may enrol you on the information the Commonwealth sends`
    `it does not reach the register: you must send a State claim`

-- The kind of election a candidate stands at (s 4: "election means a Council election or an election in a district").
DECLARE `Kind of election` IS ONE OF
    `an election in a district, for the Legislative Assembly`
    `a Council election, for the Legislative Council`

DECLARE `When my deposit is due` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `at or before the close of nominations, lodged with the returning officer`
    `not later than 24 hours before the close of nominations, lodged with the Electoral Commissioner`

DECLARE `What happens to my deposit` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it is returned to you, or to a person you authorise in writing`
    `it is returned to the person who paid it, or to a person they authorise in writing`
    `it is forfeited to the Crown`

-- The person's circumstances, as the questions ask them (Q9 in NOTES.md). The baseline reads its `My circumstances`
-- record's yes/no fields only in three groups -- citizenship (s 17(1)(a)), the s 18(2) bars on enrolment, the further
-- s 18(1) bars on voting -- each through an OR, so each group is one field here, and `my circumstances in` builds the
-- baseline's record, putting each group as its first field and the rest FALSE.
DECLARE `About me` HAS
    `my date of birth`                                                          IS A DATE
    `I am an Australian citizen, or a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice, am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a), was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned, or hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer, or am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day I began living in my district`                                     IS A DATE
    `my enrolment`                                                              IS A `My enrolment`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `a` IS AN `About me`
GIVETH A `My circumstances`
`my circumstances in` `a` MEANS `My circumstances` WITH
    `my date of birth`                                                          IS `a`'s `my date of birth`
    `I am an Australian citizen`                                                IS `a`'s `I am an Australian citizen, or a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984`
    `I am a British subject who was an elector within 3 months before 26 January 1984` IS FALSE
    `I hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen`                      IS `a`'s `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice, am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a), was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned, or hold a temporary visa or am an unlawful noncitizen`
    `I am the subject of a lack of capacity notice`                             IS FALSE
    `I am off the Commonwealth roll for this State on the ground in Commonwealth section 93(8)(a)` IS FALSE
    `I was convicted of treason and have not been pardoned`                     IS FALSE
    `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer` IS `a`'s `I am serving or yet to serve detention or imprisonment of 1 year or longer, or am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision`
    `I am under indefinite imprisonment, a Criminal Code order or supervision`  IS FALSE
    `the day I began living in my district`                                     IS `a`'s `the day I began living in my district`
    `my enrolment`                                                              IS `a`'s `my enrolment`

-- What happened at the election, built from the facts a question asks (Q9 in NOTES.md); a question passes FALSE for a
-- fact the baseline rule it calls does not read.
GIVEN `voted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `away` IS A BOOLEAN
      `impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `religious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happened at the election`
`the election for` `voted` `away` `impaired` `religious` `other reason` `satisfied` MEANS `What happened at the election` WITH
    `I voted`                                                         IS `voted`
    `I was outside the State, and that prevented me voting`           IS `away`
    `I had a mental or physical impairment on the voting days`        IS `impaired`
    `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` IS `religious`
    `I had another valid and sufficient reason`                       IS `other reason`
    `the Commissioner is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason` IS `satisfied`

-- s 196(1): "If an employee who is an elector notifies the elector's employer before polling day that the elector would
-- like a leave of absence to enable them to vote in any election, the employer must, if the absence desired is necessary
-- to enable the employee to vote in the election, allow them a leave of absence without any penalty or disproportionate
-- deduction of pay for such reasonable period not exceeding 2 hours as is necessary". (3): "This section shall not apply
-- to any elector whose absence may cause danger or substantial loss in respect of the employment".
GIVEN `the employee is an elector`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `they asked before polling day`                 IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is necessary for them to vote`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence may cause danger or substantial loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 196(1), (3) -- the employer must allow leave of absence to vote` IF
        `the employee is an elector`
    AND `they asked before polling day`
    AND `the absence is necessary for them to vote`
    AND (NOT `the absence may cause danger or substantial loss`)

-- s 196(1): "not exceeding 2 hours".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 196(1) -- the most leave to vote, in hours` MEANS 2

-- s 190: "Any contravention of this Act for which no other punishment is provided. Penalty not exceeding $1 000."
-- s 196 provides no punishment of its own, so a contravention of s 196(1) by the employer, or of s 196(2) by the
-- employee, falls under this line (INFERENCE: the Act calls neither an offence in its own words).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 190 -- the most fine for a contravention with no other punishment` MEANS 1000

-- s 81(2): "the required deposit is -- (a) in the case of an election in a district -- $250 or any greater amount that is
-- prescribed; or (b) in the case of a Council election -- $2 000 or any greater amount that is prescribed." (3): "Despite
-- subsection (2)(b), if the candidate is included in a group consisting of more than 5 candidates the required deposit is
-- the amount obtained by dividing $10 000, or any greater amount that is prescribed, by the number of candidates included
-- in the group." The Electoral Regulations 1996 are not deposited, so the Act's own amounts are used: a greater amount
-- prescribed would change the answer.
GIVEN `the election` IS A `Kind of election`
      `the number of candidates in the group` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 81(2), (3) -- the required deposit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the election`
    WHEN `an election in a district, for the Legislative Assembly` THEN 250
    WHEN `a Council election, for the Legislative Council` THEN
        IF `the number of candidates in the group` GREATER THAN 5
        THEN 10000 DIVIDED BY `the number of candidates in the group`
        ELSE 2000

-- s 84(1): the deposit "shall be returned ... if the person is elected or" the votes polled in the person's favour (in a
-- Council election, the person's or the person's group's first preferences; in a single member election, the person's
-- first preferences, or votes where there are only 2 candidates) are "more than 4%" of the total; "otherwise it shall be
-- forfeited to the Crown". (3): a candidate nominated under s 81A(2) -- the deposit is "returned to the person who paid
-- it, or to a person authorised in writing by the person who paid it". (4): "In all other cases, the deposit shall be
-- returned to the candidate, or to a person authorised in writing by the candidate". s 84(2) (a candidate who dies) is
-- not encoded.
GIVEN `I was elected`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes for me`                 IS A NUMBER
      `the total votes`                  IS A NUMBER
      `it is a party nomination`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happens to my deposit`
`s 84(1), (3), (4) -- what happens to the deposit` MEANS
    IF `I was elected` OR ((`the votes for me` TIMES 100) GREATER THAN (`the total votes` TIMES 4))
    THEN IF `it is a party nomination`
         THEN `it is returned to the person who paid it, or to a person they authorise in writing`
         ELSE `it is returned to you, or to a person you authorise in writing`
    ELSE `it is forfeited to the Crown`

§§ `For the State elector, or a person who may be entitled to enrol`

§§§ `ss 17, 17AA, 18 -- entitlement to be enrolled and to vote`

@export Have I reached a given age on a given day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 17(1)(b), 17AA(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in whole years
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I reached this age on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Have I reached the age` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the age` `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I lived in my district for at least 1 month on a given day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17(1)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I lived in my district for a month on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Have I lived in my district for a month` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I barred from being enrolled (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 18(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I barred from being enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I barred from enrolment` (`my circumstances in` `me`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I barred from voting at State elections (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 18(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I barred from voting at State elections` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I barred from voting` (`my circumstances in` `me`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Apart from my age and residence, am I qualified to be enrolled (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 17(1)(a), 18(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Apart from my age and residence, am I qualified to be enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I qualified apart from age and residence` (`my circumstances in` `me`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I entitled to be enrolled for my district on a given day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I entitled to be enrolled for my district on this day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I entitled to be enrolled` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On what day did I become entitled to be enrolled for my district (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`On what day did I become entitled to be enrolled for my district` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `on` (`On what day did I become entitled to be enrolled` (`my circumstances in` `me`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an elector on polling day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 4, 17AA(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an elector on this polling day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an elector` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I entitled to vote at a State election with this polling day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 17(1)(e), 17AA(2), 18(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I entitled to vote at this State election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I entitled to vote` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I enrol on polling day and vote as a provisional voter (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
      `I present at a place to vote and make a State or Commonwealth claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether on that day you present at a place to vote and make a claim for enrolment under this Act or under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I enrol on polling day and vote as a provisional voter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Can I enrol on polling day and vote provisionally` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day` `I present at a place to vote and make a State or Commonwealth claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I enrol for my district at 16 or 17 (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17AA(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I enrol for my district at 16 or 17` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`May I enrol at 16 or 17` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I enrolled at 16 or 17, am I treated as a silent elector on a given day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 17AA(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I treated as a silent elector because I am under 18` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Am I taken to be a silent elector because of my age` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 45 -- compulsory enrolment and a new address`

@export Must I be enrolled for my district (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be enrolled for my district` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Must I enrol` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By the end of what day must I be enrolled to avoid the offence of not being enrolled (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(1): 21 days beginning on the day I became entitled)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`By the end of what day must I be enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        CONSIDER `What is the last day by which I must be enrolled` (`my circumstances in` `me`)
        WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN `by the end of` `the last day`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `no day comes: you are not qualified to be enrolled apart from your age and residence`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(1), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
      `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove that you are not enrolled for some reason other than your own failure to send a claim
      `I am not enrolled because of a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not enrolled because you have a physical or mental impairment
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled for my district` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed the offence of not being enrolled` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day` `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` `I am not enrolled because of a physical or mental impairment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I still be prosecuted for not being enrolled (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(1), (4), (5), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
      `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can prove that you are not enrolled for some reason other than your own failure to send a claim
      `I am not enrolled because of a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are not enrolled because you have a physical or mental impairment
      `I have since sent a State claim or lodged a Commonwealth claim, or been enrolled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether since then you have sent a claim to the Electoral Commissioner, lodged a claim under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918, or been enrolled
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still be prosecuted for not being enrolled for my district` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be prosecuted for not being enrolled` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the day` `I can prove it is not because I failed to send a claim` `I am not enrolled because of a physical or mental impairment` `I have since sent a State claim or lodged a Commonwealth claim, or been enrolled`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Situation: a change of primary residential address within the district (s 45(2) runs "within 21 days after the change").
@export By when must I give written notice of my new address in the same district (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have changed my address within my district` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled and have moved your primary residential address from one address in your district to another in the same district
      `the day I moved` IS A DATE @desc The day you changed your primary residential address within your district, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`By when must I tell the Electoral Commissioner my new address` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have changed my address within my district`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by the end of` (`By when must I give notice of my new address` `the day I moved`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be prosecuted for not giving notice of my new address (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 45(2), (5), (8))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have changed my address within my district` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled and have moved your primary residential address from one address in your district to another in the same district
      `the day I moved` IS A DATE @desc The day you changed your primary residential address within your district, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the question is about, ISO 8601 (for example today, the polling day, or the day you would claim)
      `my failure to give notice is because of a physical or mental impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not given notice of the new address because you have a physical or mental impairment
      `I have since given notice or lodged a Commonwealth claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since given written notice of the new address, or lodged a claim for enrolment under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be prosecuted for not telling the Electoral Commissioner my new address` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have changed my address within my district`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be prosecuted for not notifying my new address` `the day I moved` `the day` `my failure to give notice is because of a physical or mental impairment` `I have since given notice or lodged a Commonwealth claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 31, 31A, 35A -- the Commonwealth roll and the State register`

-- Situation: being on the Commonwealth roll for an address in the State; the question asks what that enrolment does.
@export If I am enrolled on the Commonwealth roll, does that reach the State register (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 31, 31A, 35A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am on the Commonwealth roll for an address in Western Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are enrolled on the Commonwealth roll (Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918) for an address in Western Australia
      `how` IS A `How I came onto the Commonwealth roll` @desc How you came onto the Commonwealth roll for an address in Western Australia
      `a single enrolment procedure is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Gazette order under s 31(3) declares a single enrolment procedure in operation
      `an information-sharing arrangement is in operation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an arrangement under s 31A(1) for notifying direct Commonwealth enrolments is in operation
GIVETH A `Where my Commonwealth enrolment goes`
`Does my Commonwealth enrolment reach the State register of electors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I am on the Commonwealth roll for an address in Western Australia`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE CONSIDER `Does my Commonwealth enrolment reach the State register` `how` `a single enrolment procedure is in operation` `an information-sharing arrangement is in operation`
             WHEN `my claim is also my State claim, received by the Australian Electoral Officer` THEN `it reaches the register: your Commonwealth claim is also your State claim, received by the Australian Electoral Officer`
             WHEN `the Electoral Commissioner may enrol me on the notified information` THEN `it may reach the register: the Electoral Commissioner may enrol you on the information the Commonwealth sends`
             WHEN `nothing reaches it: I must send a State claim` THEN `it does not reach the register: you must send a State claim`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 156(1), (1A), (16) -- the duty to vote`

@export Must I vote at a State election with this polling day (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
      `absence from the State prevented me voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether absence from Western Australia prevented you from voting at the election (s 156(1))
      `I had a mental or physical impairment on the days of voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a mental or physical impairment on the days on which voting occurred in the election (s 156(1))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I vote at this State election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Must I vote` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day` (`the election for` FALSE `absence from the State prevented me voting` `I had a mental or physical impairment on the days of voting` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I have a valid and sufficient reason for not voting (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(1A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you honestly believe it is part of your religious duty to abstain from voting (s 156(1A))
      `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting (s 156(1A))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I have a valid and sufficient reason for not voting at this election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Do I have a valid and sufficient reason` (`the election for` FALSE FALSE FALSE `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have I committed the offence of failing to vote (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(16))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
      `I voted at the election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you voted at the election
      `absence from the State prevented me voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether absence from Western Australia prevented you from voting at the election (s 156(1))
      `I had a mental or physical impairment on the days of voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a mental or physical impairment on the days on which voting occurred in the election (s 156(1))
      `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you honestly believe it is part of your religious duty to abstain from voting (s 156(1A))
      `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting (s 156(1A))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have I committed the offence of failing to vote at this election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Have I committed the offence of failing to vote` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day` (`the election for` `I voted at the election` `absence from the State prevented me voting` `I had a mental or physical impairment on the days of voting` `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the Electoral Commissioner send me a penalty notice (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(2), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
      `I voted at the election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you voted at the election
      `absence from the State prevented me voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether absence from Western Australia prevented you from voting at the election (s 156(1))
      `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you honestly believe it is part of your religious duty to abstain from voting (s 156(1A))
      `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting (s 156(1A))
      `the Electoral Commissioner is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner is satisfied that you were absent from the State, were not entitled to vote, or had a valid and sufficient reason for not voting (s 156(4))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the Electoral Commissioner send me a penalty notice for not voting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be sent a penalty notice` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day` (`the election for` `I voted at the election` `absence from the State prevented me voting` FALSE `I honestly believe abstaining from voting is part of my religious duty` `I had another valid and sufficient reason for not voting` `the Electoral Commissioner is satisfied of my absence, ineligibility or reason`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 156(6)-(15A) -- after a penalty notice`

-- Situation: a penalty notice sent under s 156(4). Each of these seven questions turns on it.

@export Is the response date in my notice lawful (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(7), (13): at least 21 days after the notice is sent)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc The day the penalty notice or infringement notice was sent, ISO 8601
      `the response date` IS A DATE @desc The response date set out in the notice, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the response date in my notice lawful under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is the response date lawful` `the day the notice was sent` `the response date`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the modified penalty in my notice can be (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(8), (13))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `I have paid a modified penalty or been convicted under section 156 before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have previously paid a modified penalty under s 156 of this Act, or been convicted of an offence against it (a Commonwealth penalty does not count)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much at most can the modified penalty in my notice be` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most the modified penalty can be` `I have paid a modified penalty or been convicted under section 156 before`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my response to the penalty notice stop a prosecution for not voting (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(11))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `my response` IS A `My response to the penalty notice` @desc How you responded to the penalty notice by its response date
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my response to the penalty notice stop a prosecution for not voting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does my response stop a prosecution` `my response`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the Electoral Commissioner send me an infringement notice (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(12), (13A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `my response` IS A `My response to the penalty notice` @desc How you responded to the penalty notice by its response date
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the Electoral Commissioner send me an infringement notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May I be sent an infringement notice` `my response`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I still be prosecuted for failing to vote (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(11), (14), (16))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `I failed to vote without a valid and sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to vote without a valid and sufficient reason (s 156(16))
      `my response` IS A `My response to the penalty notice` @desc How you responded to the penalty notice by its response date
      `I paid the infringement notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent an infringement notice and paid its modified penalty by its response date
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I still be prosecuted for failing to vote at this election` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be prosecuted for failing to vote` `I failed to vote without a valid and sufficient reason` `my response` `I paid the infringement notice in time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I cannot respond to my notice myself, may another elector respond for me (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(14a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `I am away from my place of living or physically incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether absence from your place of living or physical incapacity stops you responding by the response date
      `they are an elector with personal knowledge of the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other person is an elector who personally knows the facts
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May another elector respond to my notice for me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`May another elector respond for me` `I am away from my place of living or physically incapacitated` `they are an elector with personal knowledge of the facts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my name be removed from the register for not responding to my notice (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 156(15), (15A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Electoral Commissioner has sent you a penalty notice (s 156(4)) because you appear not to have voted at a State election
      `I failed to respond to a penalty or infringement notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed or neglected to respond to a penalty notice or an infringement notice
      `the Commissioner is satisfied I no longer live at my roll address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that you no longer live at the address shown in the roll
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my name be removed from the register for not responding to my notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been sent a penalty notice for not voting`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my name be removed from the register` `I failed to respond to a penalty or infringement notice` `the Commissioner is satisfied I no longer live at my roll address`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 45, 156(16), (16A) -- the elector's fines`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 45(1), (2), 156(16), (16A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS A `My offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for this electoral offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 196 -- leave from work to vote`

-- Situation: being an employee. s 196(1) gives the right to "an employee who is an elector"; whether I am an elector on
-- polling day is the baseline's own answer (s 4, s 17AA(2)(a)).
@export May I have leave from work, without penalty or a disproportionate deduction of pay, for up to 2 hours to vote (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 196(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for an employer
      `me` IS A `About me` @desc Your circumstances: your date of birth, citizenship, the matters in s 18, the day you began living in your district, and your enrolment
      `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day of the State election, ISO 8601
      `I told my employer before polling day that I would like leave to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before polling day, you told your employer that you would like a leave of absence to vote
      `the absence is necessary for me to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need to be absent from work to be able to vote at the election
      `my absence may cause danger or substantial loss in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your absence may cause danger or substantial loss in respect of the employment you are engaged in (s 196(3))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I have leave from work to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I am an employee`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`s 196(1), (3) -- the employer must allow leave of absence to vote` (`Am I an elector` (`my circumstances in` `me`) `the polling day`) `I told my employer before polling day that I would like leave to vote` `the absence is necessary for me to vote` `my absence may cause danger or substantial loss in my employment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for getting leave to vote when I do not mean to vote (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 196(2), 190)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you work for an employer
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for getting leave to vote without meaning to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am, or may be entitled to be, a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `I am an employee`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `s 190 -- the most fine for a contravention with no other punishment`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the employer of an elector`

§§§ `s 196 -- leave of absence to vote`

-- Situation: an employee's request for leave to vote. s 196(1) turns on the employee's notification.

@export Must I allow my employee leave of absence to vote, without penalty or a disproportionate deduction of pay (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 196(1), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an employee has asked me for leave to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employee has told you that they would like a leave of absence to vote in a State election
      `the employee is an elector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee is enrolled as a State elector
      `they asked before polling day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee asked you before polling day
      `the absence is necessary for them to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee needs to be absent from work to be able to vote at the election
      `their absence may cause danger or substantial loss in the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employee's absence may cause danger or substantial loss in respect of the employment they are engaged in (s 196(3))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I allow my employee leave of absence to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who is a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `an employee has asked me for leave to vote`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`s 196(1), (3) -- the employer must allow leave of absence to vote` `the employee is an elector` `they asked before polling day` `the absence is necessary for them to vote` `their absence may cause danger or substantial loss in the employment`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How long a leave of absence to vote must I allow, at the most (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 196(1): a reasonable period, as is necessary to vote)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an employee has asked me for leave to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employee has told you that they would like a leave of absence to vote in a State election
GIVETH A `Hours`
`How long a leave of absence to vote must I allow at the most` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who is a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `an employee has asked me for leave to vote`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `up to` `s 196(1) -- the most leave to vote, in hours`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not allowing leave to vote (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 196(1), 190)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `an employee has asked me for leave to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employee has told you that they would like a leave of absence to vote in a State election
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for not allowing leave to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone who is a State elector` THEN
        IF NOT `an employee has asked me for leave to vote`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount `s 190 -- the most fine for a contravention with no other punishment`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the candidate`

§§§ `ss 81, 81A, 82 -- nomination and the deposit`

@export How much is the deposit I must lodge to be nominated (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 81(2), (3); unless a greater amount is prescribed)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the election I am standing in` IS A `Kind of election` @desc Whether you are standing for a district (Legislative Assembly) or at a Council election (Legislative Council)
      `the number of candidates in my group` IS A NUMBER @desc At a Council election, the number of candidates in the group you are included in (0 if you are not in a group)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is the deposit I must lodge to be nominated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN amount (`s 81(2), (3) -- the required deposit` `the election I am standing in` `the number of candidates in my group`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 81(1)(b): the deposit is lodged "at or before the close of nominations ... with the returning officer". s 81A(2)(c):
-- for a party nomination, "not later than 24 hours before the close of nominations ... with the Electoral Commissioner".
@export By when, and with whom, must my deposit be lodged (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) ss 81(1)(b), 81A(2)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my nomination is a party nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered political party nominates you, or nominated you, as its endorsed candidate under s 81A(2)
GIVETH A `When my deposit is due`
`By when and with whom must my deposit be lodged` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN
        IF `my nomination is a party nomination`
        THEN `not later than 24 hours before the close of nominations, lodged with the Electoral Commissioner`
        ELSE `at or before the close of nominations, lodged with the returning officer`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 81(1): "A nomination is not valid unless -- (a) the nomination paper is received by the returning officer after the
-- issue of the writ and before the close of nominations; and (b) at or before the close of nominations, the required
-- deposit is lodged". Only these two conditions are encoded; a nomination failing either is not valid ("not valid
-- unless"). The party nomination route (s 81A(2)) and s 79's contents of the paper are not encoded.
@export Is my nomination valid as to its paper and its deposit (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 81(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my nomination paper was received after the writ and before the close of nominations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the returning officer received your nomination paper after the issue of the writ and before the close of nominations
      `my deposit was lodged by the close of nominations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the required deposit was lodged with the returning officer by you or for you at or before the close of nominations
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my nomination valid as to its paper and its deposit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN
        `yes if` (`my nomination paper was received after the writ and before the close of nominations` AND `my deposit was lodged by the close of nominations`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 82(1): a candidate may withdraw "by lodging with the returning officer notice in writing of the withdrawal of the
-- nomination at any time before the close of nominations"; (2): "The withdrawal of the nomination of a candidate included
-- in a group has no effect unless each other candidate included in the group has consented in writing".
@export Can I withdraw my nomination (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 82)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is before the close of nominations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether nominations have not yet closed
      `I am included in a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are included in a group of candidates (s 80)
      `every other candidate in my group has consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether each other candidate in your group has consented in writing to your withdrawal
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I withdraw my nomination` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN
        `yes if` (`it is before the close of nominations` AND ((NOT `I am included in a group`) OR `every other candidate in my group has consented in writing`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 82(1): on withdrawal "the nomination is cancelled and the deposit lodged with the nomination is forfeited to the
-- Crown".
@export If I withdraw my nomination, what happens to my deposit (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 82(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `What happens to my deposit`
`If I withdraw my nomination what happens to my deposit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN `it is forfeited to the Crown`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 84 -- the deposit after the election`

-- Situation: the election held and the votes counted (s 84(1): "after the election").
@export After the election, is my deposit returned, and to whom (Electoral Act 1907 (WA) s 84(1), (3), (4): more than 4% of the votes, or elected)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the election has been held and the votes counted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the election you stood at has been held and the votes counted
      `I was elected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were elected
      `the votes for me` IS A NUMBER @desc The first preference votes polled for you (at a Council election, for you or the group you are in; where only 2 candidates stood for a single seat, the votes polled for you)
      `the total votes` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of those votes polled for all the candidates in the election
      `my nomination is a party nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered political party nominates you, or nominated you, as its endorsed candidate under s 81A(2)
GIVETH A `What happens to my deposit`
`After the election is my deposit returned and to whom` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a candidate, or want to stand, at a State election` THEN
        IF NOT `the election has been held and the votes counted`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `s 84(1), (3), (4) -- what happens to the deposit` `I was elected` `the votes for me` `the total votes` `my nomination is a party nomination`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
